1
00:00:00,402 --> 00:00:09,137
A model, a harness, and a research task. Follow how GPT five point six Sol and DeepAgents reach a checked result.

2
00:00:11,384 --> 00:00:19,605
The paper studies consumption smoothing in interwar Japan. How does household consumption respond to disposable income?

3
00:00:20,253 --> 00:00:28,431
Six pieces must agree: data, regression, fixed effects, controls, clustered standard errors, and the result file.

4
00:00:29,181 --> 00:00:37,295
The reference stays sealed. The agent must produce the coefficient, standard error, and p-value without seeing it.

5
00:00:37,931 --> 00:00:43,688
DeepAgents connects each model request to a tool, then brings observations back.

6
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:48,373
The model first asks to inspect the household panel.

7
00:00:49,002 --> 00:00:55,060
DeepAgents routes that request through run Python, the tool used for this recorded run.

8
00:00:56,145 --> 00:01:03,445
The sandbox reads the Stata file. Shape, columns, and household counts flow back to the model.

9
00:01:05,074 --> 00:01:11,602
Eighteen eighty rows, sixty-three columns, four quarters, and two hundred thirty-seven households.

10
00:01:12,663 --> 00:01:18,249
Using that observation, the model asks what packages and samples are available.

11
00:01:18,884 --> 00:01:25,455
DeepAgents routes another run Python request, carrying the next data and environment checks.

12
00:01:26,086 --> 00:01:34,093
The sandbox checks installed packages, missing values, and observations per household, then returns the findings.

13
00:01:34,747 --> 00:01:47,297
Linearmodels, statsmodels, and scipy are available. Pyreadstat is missing. All eleven variables are complete, averaging seven point nine three observations per household.

14
00:01:47,931 --> 00:01:52,702
The next request compares regression methods and standard errors.

15
00:01:53,348 --> 00:02:00,155
The request includes fixed effects, composition-by-quarter controls, and household-clustered errors.

16
00:02:00,788 --> 00:02:08,709
Run Python evaluates the variants in the sandbox. Their outputs become evidence for the next model decision.

17
00:02:09,359 --> 00:02:20,131
The coefficient stays near zero point three nine one eight six five. Four methods give different standard errors. The small-sample correction matters.

18
00:02:20,758 --> 00:02:24,908
The model follows up by asking for variable labels.

19
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:31,157
DeepAgents routes this fourth run Python request to inspect the Stata metadata.

20
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:39,315
Pandas inspects labels and notes in the same data file. The tool brings these observations back to the model.

21
00:02:39,955 --> 00:02:50,512
H I D means household ID. T F E is the year-month count. Quarter maps the survey periods, and disposable income is measured in yen.

22
00:02:51,145 --> 00:02:57,845
The harness routed every earlier step. Now this evaluation's tool budget is reached.

23
00:02:58,497 --> 00:03:01,639
The model proposes one more check.

24
00:03:02,276 --> 00:03:06,812
It requests another Panel OLS fit with a group adjustment.

25
00:03:07,455 --> 00:03:16,362
All four allowed tool calls are used. This evaluation's budget guard rejects the fifth request and asks for the final program.

26
00:03:17,008 --> 00:03:20,922
The sixth model call prepares the final submission.

27
00:03:21,562 --> 00:03:30,919
The submitted main dot py contains demeaning, regression, clustered correction, and JSON-writing logic. It has not run yet.

28
00:03:31,562 --> 00:03:35,283
An independent evaluator now takes over.

29
00:03:35,937 --> 00:03:43,751
The independent evaluator runs main dot py. This execution writes the required result JSON.

30
00:03:44,389 --> 00:03:51,668
The program exits successfully and saves a valid prediction: coefficient, standard error, and p-value.

31
00:03:52,305 --> 00:03:59,048
The reference is revealed. The coefficient passes its one-percent relative-error tolerance.

32
00:03:59,686 --> 00:04:04,522
The standard error also passes the one-percent relative-error check.

33
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:10,812
The p-value passes a separate absolute-error tolerance of zero point zero one.

34
00:04:11,443 --> 00:04:20,671
All three pass. The earlier dummy-variable standard error would fail. Within tolerance does not mean identical digits.

35
00:04:21,323 --> 00:04:31,259
Complete reproduction: six model calls, four tool calls, forty-six thousand four hundred ninety-six tokens, and about two minutes of recorded runtime.

36
00:04:32,037 --> 00:04:44,137
DeepAgents connects decisions, tools, and observations. The evaluator checks the result. This trace shows one complete workflow, not a ranking of harnesses.
